where a value is kept. Importing a target enters its phony name and nothing else. Once
the makefiles are read, and only when some body holds a reference, the directory and a
value file for each referenced target are entered; a referenced target reruns when a
value it reads is newer, and its name prints what is kept. A plain file is read where it
is, never copied. Any other imported target runs whenever it is asked for, on the job's
own standard input and output, and the goal function reads what that run printed. One
